  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35733894",
      "title": "Onwards to a new Project Setup",
      "sourceHash": "9c56a41d6019525b146a34f765effd5e34bb8eae08ac426d7ec8b68b2dd431ad",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 3.33,
          "en": "At this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.33,
          "end": 6.06,
          "en": "you already learned a lot about routing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.06,
          "end": 8.04,
          "en": "and we had a thorough look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.04,
          "end": 10.86,
          "en": "at all the key routing features you must know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.86,
          "end": 13.2,
          "en": "Now, over the next lectures,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.2,
          "end": 15.6,
          "en": "we're going to dive deeper into routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.6,
          "end": 18.9,
          "en": "and explore more advanced routing features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.9,
          "end": 22.59,
          "en": "especially related to data fetching and submission.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.59,
          "end": 26.58,
          "en": "But before we do so, it's time to practice what you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.58,
          "end": 30.7,
          "en": "Now for that, you find the never project attached,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.7,
          "end": 34.53,
          "en": "and this project actually includes two project folders:",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.53,
          "end": 38.49,
          "en": "a backend-api and a react-frontend folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.49,
          "end": 41.07,
          "en": "You also got a file with some instructions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.07,
          "end": 43.92,
          "en": "But in the end, this backend-api folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.92,
          "end": 47.61,
          "en": "simply includes a dummy backend application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.61,
          "end": 50.61,
          "en": "that does not contain any React code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.61,
          "end": 53.61,
          "en": "that will be used throughout this course section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.61,
          "end": 57.15,
          "en": "so that we have a dummy backend to work with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.15,
          "end": 59.67,
          "en": "We could also use some public service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.67,
          "end": 62.91,
          "en": "like Firebase or some public dummy API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.91,
          "end": 67.68,
          "en": "but here I built this custom dummy API which we'll use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.68,
          "end": 69.78,
          "en": "But you won't have to write any code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.78,
          "end": 72.15,
          "en": "in this backend-API folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.15,
          "end": 73.65,
          "en": "This is provided for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.65,
          "end": 75.57,
          "en": "It's not related to React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.57,
          "end": 78.3,
          "en": "And you can, of course, explore that code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.3,
          "end": 80.16,
          "en": "but you don't have to understand it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.16,
          "end": 83.64,
          "en": "It's NoteExpress code not related to React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.64,
          "end": 87.75,
          "en": "But we will be able to send requests to that backend-api",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.75,
          "end": 90.6,
          "en": "from inside our React app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.6,
          "end": 94.08,
          "en": "Now, very important, in the react-frontend folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.08,
          "end": 95.88,
          "en": "you then find the React app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.88,
          "end": 99,
          "en": "on which we'll work throughout this course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99,
          "end": 102.06,
          "en": "You will see that there I already added some components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.06,
          "end": 104.55,
          "en": "which we'll use throughout this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.55,
          "end": 106.32,
          "en": "in which you, of course, can explore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.32,
          "end": 107.15299999999999,
          "en": "In the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.15299999999999,
          "end": 110.34,
          "en": "these are all relatively straightforward components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.34,
          "end": 112.97999999999999,
          "en": "with some default styling provided.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.97999999999999,
          "end": 115.83,
          "en": "And for the rest of this section, as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.83,
          "end": 119.75999999999999,
          "en": "we're going to dive deeper into routing with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.75999999999999,
          "end": 122.01,
          "en": "Now, one important note right away,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.01,
          "end": 124.89,
          "en": "you will need to start this backend server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 124.89,
          "end": 127.11,
          "en": "and this frontend server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 127.11,
          "end": 128.7,
          "en": "independent from each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.7,
          "end": 131.61,
          "en": "So you will need to open your terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.61,
          "end": 134.58,
          "en": "and navigate into the backend-api folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 134.58,
          "end": 137.61,
          "en": "initially run npm install there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 137.61,
          "end": 140.76,
          "en": "And then run npm start to start that backend server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 140.76,
          "end": 142.68,
          "en": "and keep that process running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 142.68,
          "end": 146.7,
          "en": "as long as you are working on this overall project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 146.7,
          "end": 148.8,
          "en": "You can, of course, then quit it thereafter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 148.8,
          "end": 150.15,
          "en": "with Control + C,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 150.15,
          "end": 152.97,
          "en": "but you should always restart that backend server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 152.97,
          "end": 154.8,
          "en": "in the backend-api folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 154.8,
          "end": 156.63,
          "en": "whenever you wanna go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 156.63,
          "end": 158.82,
          "en": "to working on that react-frontend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 158.82,
          "end": 160.23,
          "en": "because that frontend later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 160.23,
          "end": 162.57,
          "en": "must be able to talk to that backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 162.57,
          "end": 164.16,
          "en": "And for that, the backend server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 164.16,
          "end": 165.483,
          "en": "must be up and running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 166.5,
          "end": 168.99,
          "en": "And in a separate terminal window,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 168.99,
          "end": 171.48,
          "en": "you also must install all the dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 171.48,
          "end": 174.21,
          "en": "for the react-frontend application initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 174.21,
          "end": 175.14,
          "en": "And you, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 175.14,
          "end": 179.28,
          "en": "also must start the react-frontend dev server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 179.28,
          "end": 182.46,
          "en": "in order to work on this React application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 182.46,
          "end": 185.28,
          "en": "So both servers, backend and frontend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 185.28,
          "end": 187.983,
          "en": "should be up and running for this course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 189,
          "end": 191.37,
          "en": "And with that, that's the project setup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 191.37,
          "end": 194.253,
          "en": "Now, let's dive into these projects.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
